course: dictionary
lesson: 10485
title: Turkey: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. The word turkey can be a bird, a meal, a country, or even a failure. Read the sentence first, then decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Çatalhöyük in Turkey was a town about 9,000 years ago.» The capital T and the word "in" before a place name tell you this is the country. Test it: if you put "bird" in the sentence, it makes no sense, so the country is the right meaning.
explain: «The real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey and covered in feathers.» Here the bird is used to compare size, so turkey means the bird. Informal phrases can change the meaning again: «go cold turkey» means to stop a habit suddenly and completely.
fact: Turkey (the bird) is a large farm bird with a red, wobbly piece of skin on its neck.
fact: Turkey (the meat) is often eaten at Christmas or Thanksgiving.
fact: Turkey with a capital T is a country between Europe and Asia, and its capital is Ankara.
fact: In informal American English, a turkey can be a failure, like a very bad film or show.
fact: «Go cold turkey» means to stop a habit suddenly and completely, and «talk turkey» means to talk seriously.
exercise: «Turkey's capital is Ankara, chosen in 1923.» In this sentence, what is Turkey? | Meat for a roast | A failure, like a bad film | A large farm bird | *A country between Europe and Asia
exercise: «The real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey and covered in feathers.» What is a turkey here? | *A large bird | A habit you can stop | A country | A failure
exercise: Dad says, «I'm going cold turkey on sweets.» What does he mean? | *He is stopping eating sweets suddenly and completely | He is eating a roast turkey | He is visiting Turkey | He is buying a bird
test: «Europe has about 44 to 50 countries, depending on whether partly European countries such as Russia, Turkey and Kazakhstan are counted.» In this sentence, Turkey is | A Christmas meal | *A country | A farm bird | A bad film
test: Mum says, «Let's talk turkey about the holiday plans.» What does she mean? | Let's buy a bird for dinner | Let's stop a bad habit suddenly | Let's visit Ankara | *Let's talk seriously about the plans
exam: «The trick is to start from the sharpest clue: "my capital was chosen in 1923 and my biggest city sits on two continents" points straight at Turkey.» What does this tell you about the word Turkey? | It is a farm bird | It is a Christmas meal | *It is a country, and the clues about its capital and continents show it | It is a failure
